# DRAFT profile of the 1K run on 11 VMs (1 master, 10 workers; the rule of 9 November 2026), part 1 (the repository as pushed): ONE crawl round over the 908 seeds of profile-seeds.txt (the 1K list of teammate S minus the 92 that the seed rule of tc-crawl.sh refuses).
# NUM_FETCHERS and NUM_TASKS are 10, one fetch task per worker. NUM_THREADS=50 is teammate S's value (50 fetch threads per worker).
# SIZE_FETCHLIST is divided by the number of tasks (mistake 243): 10000 / 10 = 1000 per task, more than all 908 seeds together, so no uneven split can cut a seed.
# TIME_LIMIT_FETCH=30 minutes is teammate S value for 1K (source-provenance/bench/BENCHMARK.md: 30 / 120 / 600 minutes for 1K / 10K / 100K).
ROUNDS=1
NUM_FETCHERS=10
NUM_TASKS=10
SIZE_FETCHLIST=10000
NUM_THREADS=50
TIME_LIMIT_FETCH=30
MAP_MEMORY_MB=2048
MAP_JAVA_OPTS=-Xmx1536m
REDUCE_MEMORY_MB=2048
REDUCE_JAVA_OPTS=-Xmx1536m
HDFS_SEED_DIR=/tc/seeds
HDFS_CRAWL_DIR=/tc/crawl
WAIT_FOR_CLUSTER_SECONDS=600
MIN_FETCHED=500
AGENT_NAME=training-custody-test-bot
AGENT_URL=https://github.com/Heron-AI-Security
WARC_SOFTWARE=Apache-Nutch-CommonCrawl-fork-training-custody
